      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — removing unused imports and the unused `DELTA` constant, naming the iteration count expressively, and adding a clear failure message to the assertion.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused imports (`assertArrayEquals`, `assertEquals`, `assertNotEquals` from `LangAssertions`, `assertNotNull`, `assertTrue`) and the unused `DELTA` constant; extracted `rangeSize` as a named intermediate to clarify the iteration-count arithmetic; moved the bug context into a class-level Javadoc; and added a descriptive failure message to `assertNotEquals`."
